      "post_date": "Mon Jul 26, 2004 12:47 pm",
      "post_datetime": "2004-07-26T17:47:00+00:00",
      "post_subject": "Harp Lady",
      "content_md": "No, we inherited it. We have a studio in an industrial park. The previous owner of the site was also a holographer (Don Broadbent, for those who know him). When we took over from Don, we inherited some models he left behind. Mostly they're in a series of boxes in a loft area which we rarely go into. Last week we felt we had to do two \"honour holograms\", one for the kitsch competition for Tom (on it's way, Tom!) and one to thank Colin for his hospitality during our recent visit to Napa. While rummaging through the case of objects, I came across Harp Lady and thought that Colin would like it because of the musical connotation.",
